1600 BM$="Woman: Oh my, Susanna! You're here early! When you said you were coming\with David, I thought it would take you a few more days...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1610 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: It's been a long time, Mrs. Emily. There's a reason we're here so\early... Is Mr. Lands here?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1620 BM$="Emily: He is. Come on in.\You must be David. I'm Lands's wife, Emily. Please, make yourself at home.":GOSUB 5100
1630 GOSUB 6190:BM$="Before David could even reply, Emily went back inside to call her husband.\Susanna led him inside.":GOSUB 5100
1640 GOSUB 6180:BM$="Lands came out of one of the rooms with his wife.":GOSUB 5100
1650 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Emily: See, Susanna brought David here. David, this is my husband, Lands.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1660 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I'm David. Sorry to barge in without notice.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1670 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: Mr. Lands, I... messed up. The King of the North knows about David,\and he's hunting him.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1680 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Lands: I see... Last night I was reading the energy of the star of darkness,\and the candle flame flickered violently. I knew it was a bad omen...":GOSUB 5100
1690 BM$="Lands: I never would've imagined the King of the North himself was after\you. Tell me more.":GOSUB 5100
1700 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna told him everything; from the letter David received from the\reporter Connors, to the suspicion that the King of the North might be\Archbishop Mellis of St. Radford's Church.":GOSUB 5100
1710 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Lands: So that's why we lost contact with the sorcerers in London... We\tried to warn them about the impending doom, but the northern tribes\must have found them first...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1720 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: I'm afraid you, Mr. Holly, and Mr. Greg are the only dark sorcerers\left in England. It's up to us to revive the power of the Devil King sleeping\in David's blood.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1730 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Lands: Holly's powers are too weak. We can only count on Greg... It's true\that the power of the Devil King could easily defeat the King of the North,\but we need to shed the blood of the northern tribes.":GOSUB 5100:BM$="I'm not sure we can do this alone...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1740 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: We know where the King of the North is. With some planning, we\should be able to capture a northern tribesman.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1750 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Lands: That might have been possible when he didn't know about us yet, but\now?":GOSUB 5100
1760 BM$="Lands: I think you should leave England and wait until the star of darkness\leaves Earth. This isn't just about fighting. We must also think about\protecting the bloodline.":GOSUB 5100
1770 BM$="Lands: We've been protecting the bloodline without fighting for\generations. We have our backs against the wall... There's nothing we can\do now. Not even King Hroth would fight in this situation.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1780 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: Are you asking us to run away from the King of the North? If we\did that, our children would have to suffer the same fate. No, we have to\kill the King of the North while we have a chance.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1790 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Lands: Once the energy of the star of darkness is gone, both the northern\and the dark sorcerers will return to a normal life. We wouldn't have to\worry about the King of the North for the next 300 years.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1800 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: Let's go back to my mother's castle and think about it. Please call\Mr. Greg, I'd like to hear his opinion as well. I'm still convinced that we could\capture a northern tribesman.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
